#
# The Ruby every Windows job and the Windows pre-push checks run
# (.github/windows_ruby.sh). RubyInstaller publishes no Ruby 4.1 preview,
# and its head build is rebuilt from Ruby's master every day under one
# URL, so a Windows gem built on one day's head need not load in another
# day's: each day's ABI can differ (RbConfig::CONFIG["ruby_version"],
# such as 4.1.0+6). Fledge keeps a copy of the head build its Windows
# runtime is made from, and this pins that copy, by its SHA-256, so
# Lota's Windows gems are built and tested on the Ruby that runs them in
# a fused app (ADR 013). Move it with Lota::Fuse::FLEDGE_REF.
#
# For each architecture: the 7z's URL, its SHA-256, and the
# ruby_version that Ruby must report.
x64_url=https://github.com/setdef/Fledge/releases/download/inputs-rubyinstaller-head-20261110/rubyinstaller-head-x64.7z
x64_sha256=901473edafd6b174d79978fc109d3df3ab73b1436719233f35c1a31b5b18bf58
x64_ruby_version=4.1.0+6
arm64_url=https://github.com/setdef/Fledge/releases/download/inputs-rubyinstaller-head-20261110/rubyinstaller-head-arm.7z
arm64_sha256=7d1ae764cc530ded0ae7f0c6e610eea17c7ef4ce574e529963072674dc234b34
arm64_ruby_version=4.1.0+6
